  "reviewed_metadata_corrections_sha256": {},
  "semantic_review": "Root read the original full Python source, all nine final additive modules, all six probe scripts and compilation/staging/freeze scripts. The four concrete grid theorems discharge their generic execution step with actual original per-program execution on evolving memory, preserving input regions and arbitrary undefined padding. Full logical frames and row/column ownership follow actual grid coordinates. Host dimension normalization, source heuristics, positive shape domain, exact metadata primitive composition, produced-output saving and backward consumption are connected. Saved output/gradient aliasing is allowed without overwriting saved values. Every autotune trial executes on prior memory and preserves inputs/undef, so the final selected launch has the independently stated pre-trial reference. Cold and cache-hit admission keeps first fp64 fallback compiler rejection and cannot replace all trials by a runnable final choice. The unused tl.cidv helper rejects if directly invoked. M/N zero errors are represented abstractly and original AST probes retain allocation order; K=0 has an explicit unsafe source path. Metadata callbacks supply only actual Torch contiguous/empty_like stride lists, including noncanonical singleton strides, and no kernel value or launch success oracle. The two public statements explicitly use real dtype erasure; the wider helper includes frontend-rejected profiles, while the primary theorem requires actual profile admission. This does not close typed floating arithmetic or finite source scalar/pointer/view domains, and no false real=floating numerical assumption is registered. Root independently replayed all host/heuristic/frontend/autotune/alias/layout/helper probes; GPU execution and timing/resource behavior remain untested.",
